# The public half of the release signing key (ed25519, PEM).
#
# Releases published by .github/workflows/release.yml are signed with the
# private half, held as the repository secret CXCG_RELEASE_SIGNING_KEY. Once a
# key is pasted here, this installation (and every later version built with it)
# installs only releases whose signature verifies against it.
#
# Until then it is empty and updates are checked against their file list only
# (marked "unsigned" on Settings -> Updates). To set it up once:
#   python backend/scripts/release_keygen.py
# then paste the printed "-----BEGIN PUBLIC KEY-----" block below these comments,
# and store the private key file's contents as the CXCG_RELEASE_SIGNING_KEY secret.
# CXCG_UPDATE_PUBLIC_KEY (the PEM text) overrides this file.
